cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Astraios in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "Astraios: free GPU-accelerated astrophotography processing"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Astraios contributors"
    alias: majmichu1
repository-code: "https://github.com/majmichu1/Astraios"
url: "https://majmichu1.github.io/Astraios/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.1.25"
date-released: "2026-08-25"
keywords:
  - astrophotography
  - image processing
  - image stacking
  - GPU
  - PyTorch
abstract: >-
  Astraios is a free, open-source desktop application for calibrating,
  registering, stacking and processing deep-sky, planetary and solar
  astrophotography on Windows, Linux and macOS, using NVIDIA CUDA or Apple
  Metal acceleration with automatic CPU fallback. The project was formerly
  known as Cosmica.
